  "description": "<iframe src=\"\" style=\"background-image: url('https://deadface.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/2026/img/wayfinder/cerealkiller04.jpg');background-size:cover;background-position:center center;background-origin:content-box;background-repeat:no-repeat;background-color:rgba(40, 40, 40,0);min-height:80px;height:130px;width:100%;padding:10px;border:none\" title=\"Thumbnail\"></iframe>\r\n<sup>Created By: <code>@TheZeal0t</code></sup>\r\n\r\nWe have a new set of Spooky Cereals this year, in honor of our New Visitors, who have traveled so long and far to come visit us and to share their other-worldly wisdom with us!\r\n\r\nFinally, we have the Greys. Everyone is very familiar with them, primarily because of Hollywood. Big eyes, big bulbous heads with skinny bodies... tiny little mouths and long, spindly fingers. You get the picture.\r\n\r\nUnlike the rest of our Far-Flung Friends, the Greys communicate with each other using \"Assembly Codes\". This has led some to speculate that they are actually biologic meat-puppets that are remotely piloted. Lytton Labs hasn't quite figured out how to talk to them... which is very unfortunate, because they kind of like to ... probe ... their \"guests\", and they don't seem to pick up on English, such as, \"OW, that @#$@#%^^ HURTS!!!\"\r\n\r\nWe have recovered a binary from one of their crashed ships, and we'd like you to analyze it. Once we figure out their favorite spooky cereal, we feel like we can better bond with our new friends!\r\n\r\nSubmit the answer as `deadface{I-For-One-Welcome-Our-New-Buggy-Overlords}` ... which is not the REAL FLAG, by the way.\r\n\r\n[Download Windows 64-bit Binary](https://tinyurl.com/yds6ucbs)(14KB)<br>\r\n<sup>SHA256: `045f72d2027c0c9397d136375341b4c5d6b9bb6765a73aa75fd3955bbef2f96f`</sup>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
